{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.Wigner2Coefficient","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.Wigner2Coefficient","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.self_conjugate_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.self_conjugate_trace","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wigner-2-coefficient.lean#L77-L101","doc":"The self-conjugate trace theorem:\nif λ = λ' with dim d, then tr(σ_g)/d = h/2.\n\nCombines paired_sum_identity with sum_involution_double. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.sum_involution_double","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.sum_involution_double","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wigner-2-coefficient.lean#L54-L75","doc":"**Involution doubling**: if σ is an involution on a Finset and\nf(i) + f(σ(i)) = c for all i, then 2 · Σf = |S| · c.\n\nProof: Σf∘σ = Σf (reindex by bijection), so 2Σf = Σ(f + f∘σ) = Σc. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.paired_sum_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.paired_sum_identity","kind":"theorem","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wigner-2-coefficient.lean#L29-L52","doc":"**Paired sum identity**: a_ρ + a_{-ρ} = h.\n\nThe algebraic core of the self-conjugate trace theorem. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.a_rho","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.a_rho","kind":"def","line":23,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wigner-2-coefficient.lean#L23-L27","doc":"Seminormal diagonal entry: a_ρ = h/(1 - q^{-2ρ}).\nArchimedean specialisation per AGENTS.md §7c — q : ℝ throughout\nthis block (sibling .md narrative carries the §7c banner). ","signatureChunk":0}]}